      \field{abstract}{This book provides a comprehensive examination of biocontrol methods for agricultural protection. It discusses the necessity of sustainable agricultural practices, focusing on biocontrol as an innovative alternative to synthetic pesticides. The text explores various techniques, including biological control using natural predators, the use of microbiomes to enhance plant health, and the application of biopesticides. The authors aim to present biocontrol as a viable and effective solution for managing pests and diseases, highlighting its ecological benefits and potential for large-scale implementation. The book targets agricultural scientists, policymakers, and practitioners interested in sustainable agriculture}
